.TH PBWATCH 1 "2026-10-23" "pbwatch 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
pbwatch \- battery and ANC monitor for Google Pixel Buds on Linux
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pbwatch
[\fB\-\-mac\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-\-on\-update\fR \fICOMMAND\fR]
[\fB\-\-on\-disconnect\fR \fICOMMAND\fR]
[\fB\-\-heal\-audio\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-notify\fR]
[\fB\-\-legacy\-state\-files\fR]
[\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fInotify\fR]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpbwatch\fR is a background daemon that connects to Google Pixel Buds over
Bluetooth RFCOMM and sends a desktop notification whenever battery levels or
ANC mode change.
.PP
Configuration is read from \fI~/.config/pbwatch/config.toml\fR on startup.
Command-line options override the config file.
.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B notify
Send a desktop notification with the current Pixel Buds state, then exit.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mac\fR \fIADDRESS\fR
Bluetooth MAC address of the Pixel Buds to monitor
(e.g.\& \fIAB:CD:EF:01:23:45\fR).
May be repeated for multiple pairs.
Overrides the \fBmacs\fR field in config.toml.
Find addresses with \fBbluetootlctl devices\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-update\fR \fICOMMAND\fR
Shell command to execute on battery, ANC, or placement changes.
The command receives the current state as JSON on stdin.
If omitted, pbwatch renders and sends a notification internally.
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-disconnect\fR \fICOMMAND\fR
Shell command to execute when the earbuds disconnect.
Receives the last known state as JSON on stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-heal\-audio
On connect, switch the Bluetooth card to the A2DP (high-quality audio) profile
and set it as the default audio output.
Requires \fBwireplumber\fR and \fBpulseaudio-utils\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-notify
Disable desktop notifications and hooks.
State files are still written (see \fBFILES\fR below).
.TP
.B \-\-legacy\-state\-files
Write battery and ANC state as flat files for compatibility with older scripts.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print raw RFCOMM frames to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of options and exit.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pbwatch/config.toml
User configuration file.
Created automatically with sane defaults on first run.
.TP
.I /usr/share/pbwatch/themes.json
System-wide colour theme definitions.
Can be overridden by a user copy at
.IR ~/.config/pbwatch/themes.json .
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls log verbosity.
Accepted values: \fBerror\fR, \fBwarn\fR, \fBinfo\fR (default), \fBdebug\fR, \fBtrace\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the base directory for configuration files.
Defaults to \fI~/.config\fR.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
.
